empt; preserve failures and partial timeout output. Bound each process-tree timeout by the remaining authorised check budget, retaining any integration/verification reserve. Do not substitute pytest-reported duration or rounded shell seconds for required process-wall accounting. If accounting is missing, recover existing evidence and report uncertainty; do not rerun to reconstruct it or assume authority remains. This adds no numerical execution authority or acceptance gate.\r\n- A limit-reached run or missing handoff is incomplete unless inspected evidence satisfies the task. Inspect partial artifacts and remaining execution authority before a focused continuation; return actionable findings to the same owner with a delta brief when available. If required verification cannot fit the remaining budget, preserve the candidate and report the unmet gate; do not waive checks or renew authority. Continue the same owner from useful artifacts with missing context or actionable findings; a turn limit alone does not justify takeover. Astra takes over when execution is unreliable, the owner is unavailable, or a concrete coupling, confidentiality or reserved-decision boundary requires it; record the reason briefly. Narrow work after repeated unfinished runs; extend turn limits only for demonstrated progress within remaining authority, preserving prior failures and required checks. Classify service failure, intentional interruption, turn exhaustion, implementation defects and verification-evidence gaps separately; absent checks are not disobedience when execution was prohibited. If interrupted before checkpointing, Astra preserves the logs and reconstructs actual progress. Limits are execution bounds, not guaranteed token caps.\n\n# Worker entry points\n\nUse the wrappers (PowerShell 7):\n\n```powershell\n& \"$HOME\\bin\\mistral-worker.ps1\" `\n    -Repo \"<absolute repository root>\" -Mode <Read|Edit> `\n    -Task \"<bounded outcome, ownership and contracts>\" -MaxTurns <N>\n\n& \"$HOME\\bin\\opencode-worker.ps1\" `\n    -Repo \"<absolute repository root>\" -Mode <Read|Edit> `\n    -Task \"<bounded task>\" -MaxSteps <N> -TimeoutSeconds <N>\n```\n\nOmit local `-Model` for the configured default, or supply `-Model \"<configured local provider/model>\"`; do not hard-code today's model into policy. Do not download models, reconfigure the server or switch local-only data to cloud inference without authorisation. Follow each wrapper's actual permission contract.\n\nThe local wrapper supports configured OpenAI-compatible loopback HTTP(S) providers, pins worker/helper inference to the selected model and disables sharing/external plugins. Its application permissions are not an OS sandbox or complete network isolation. Read denies edits; both modes deny unlisted tools/commands, nested workers, network tools and external directories except OpenCode's internal tool-output directory. Environment-file protections remain intact; Edit permits only owned repository edits.\n\nThe default shell allowlist contains specific Git inspections. Add `-AllowedCommands @('<exact authorised command>')` only for needed Read inspections or relevant Edit checks; never bypass failures with arbitrary interpreters, shell composition, wildcards or Git integration commands. Logs stay outside repositories; local `-OutputDirectory` selects a new evidence directory.\n\nQueue short local jobs through the wrapper's shared local-server slot. `-QueueWaitSeconds` bounds waiting separately (default 15 seconds; 0 for immediate fallback); `-TimeoutSeconds` starts when the process launches after acquiring the slot. `LOCAL_QUEUE_BUSY` means no inference started: use suitable Mistral/OpenAI when waiting would delay delivery, respecting local-only constraints, or defer. Queue records preserve wait/execution timing. This coordinates cooperating wrappers, not direct Ollama clients; do not bypass the queue or repeatedly retry a busy slot. Prefer short local jobs over long audits. Use proportionate Mistral `MaxTurns`, local agent `MaxSteps` and local process-tree `TimeoutSeconds`.\n\n# Availability and fallback\n\nLocal models and Mistral are optional dependencies. Local services/models/hardware/tools may be unavailable or unreliable; Mistral may have startup, authentication, transport, context, inference, rate-limit or allowance failures. Treat exhausted Mistral usage as unavailable for the current task.\n\nCheck availability only when useful, using one small bounded Read task through the wrapper and inspecting successful tool outcomes. A launcher, running service, CLI version, plausible answer or zero exit code alone is insufficient. Reuse established availability; do not probe before every assignment. Retain cached unavailability/exhaustion for the current task until new evidence warrants a useful attempt; do not repeatedly retry the same failure or probe unrelated workers.\n\nIf local is unavailable, use suitable Mistral/OpenAI; if Mistral is unavailable, use OpenAI; if both are unavailable, Astra continues directly. Preserve useful partial work and failed evidence. Optional workers must not block delivery or silently relax local-only constraints. Report availability when it affects the requested workflow, confidence, scope or timing. Identify any required local or independent gate left unmet; fallback does not establish different-family independence.\n\n# Verification and acceptance\n\nAfter every Edit worker, inspect Git status/diff, confirm ownership and preserved dirty work, independently run or inspect relevant checks, and resolve unexpected changes or failures. For behavior-changing repairs, confirm regression coverage of the affected contracts, including refusal, mutation and cancellation paths where relevant; add focused tests when existing coverage is insufficient. Helpers alone do not prove caller or production-path integration. Require evidence for important test-pass claims. Check consequential Read findings against source, data, equations or runtime state. For local runs, inspect effective model routing, permissions/steps and actual tool outcomes in saved logs.\n\nFor useful independent review of consequential OpenAI implementation, numerics, mechanics contracts or difficult debugging, prefer an available Mistral Read reviewer; a suitable local model may provide supporting independent input. Prefer different model families; OpenCode is a runner, not a family. Give the artifact and question without Astra's preferred answer unless that answer is under review. Seek errors, counterexamples, unsupported assumptions and missing tests; review complete slices with evidence rather than redundant/trivial fragments. An implementation author cannot supply its sole required independent assessment.\n\nResolve disagreement through underlying evidence and a discriminating check when practical. Preserve scientific gates, physical assumptions, tolerances, failed evidence, consumed authority, release restrictions and unresolved uncertainty. Worker reports and model agreement are evidence, not acceptance; Astra owns final acceptance and user-facing handoff.\r\n", "durationMs": 0.0, "display": {"success": true, "verb": "Ran", "message": "cat \"C:/Users/AudunArnesenNyhus/.codex/AGENTS.md\" 2>/dev/null | head -100", "warnings": [], "approvalNote": null, "suffix": ""}, "decision": "execute", "approvalType": "always", "approvalSource": "bypass"}}
