{"id": "reasoning-f766e208-603b-5b85-871a-777b40256931-0", "sessionId": "e897bfe5-092a-b890-fcc0-de4fff631517", "turnId": "turn-724056f1119cdc7390906102fb9abb3c", "createdAt": 1792488374995, "updatedAt": 1792488374995, "generationStatus": "completed", "relatedEntryId": null, "type": "reasoning", "text": "Now the docs update. The task:\n\n\"Docs/changelog: correct stale no-completed-plastic claim to demonstrated default -11/60m S355 case with restart; original-.20m, director stopped-1/6m and analytical accuracy remain open. Preserve experimental status, strictbool/default/positional behavior and .converged meaning. Explain achieved displacement from result.displacements/probe DOF and steps[-1].control_value for DC; .converged alone is not completion.\"\n\nCurrent \"Evidence and limits\" section says: \"Plastic coupled displacement-control continuation/restart remains incomplete in the current Slice3 evidence; completed target cases have not been established.\" — this is the stale claim to correct.\n\nNew text for Evidence and limits:\n- Default rotating route demonstrated completion of the registered S355 case to the revised -11/60 m endpoint with the public initial-state restart (6 steps to -0.10, resume 5 steps); original -0.20 m target not completed; director route stops at -1/6 m (three tests fail as record); analytical accuracy gate remains open.\n- Keep: nonmatching interpolation accuracy, case-specific verification, offset/finite rotation differences.\n- Keep .converged warning.\n- Add \"Reading a result\" guidance: status, stop_reason, achieved displacement from result.displacements at probe DOF; for displacement control steps[-1].control_value is the achieved controlled value; .converged alone is not completion; checkpoint restart requires terminal status completed; manual continuation route via initial_displacements/initial_element_states with equilibrate_initial_state=False.\n\nAlso mention the new example: examples/beam_shell_coupling.py with CLI. Add a s